---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Corrections"
  description="How Runtime Signals handles factual errors and material updates."
  canonicalPath="/corrections"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p>
    <h1>How we correct the record</h1>
    <p>
      When a published claim turns out to be wrong, outdated, or missing an important limitation, we
      fix it in place. The article keeps its URL. The fix carries a visible revision note and an
      updated timestamp, and the original claim is never quietly edited away.
    </p>
    <p>
      Retiring a piece — because a tool it covers no longer exists, or its practice no longer holds
      — is a separate action from a correction. Retired pieces are marked archived, stay reachable
      at their original URL with a notice, and drop out of the active feed and search index.
    </p>
    <p>
      No article moves in either direction without human review; a routine content or dependency fix
      does not require the same review a factual correction does, but neither is automated end to
      end.
    </p>
    <p>
      No corrections have been published yet — this repository is at its Phase 2 product foundation
      checkpoint, before any content has shipped.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-5) var(--space-9);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }
  .prose h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
